  "text": "The abstracts of all eight chapters of Nidana Sthana are presented here for introductory knowledge about its chapters. For more knowledge, the readers can go to the individual chapters.\n\nContents\n\n1 Chapter 1. Chapter on Fundamental Principles of Diagnosis and Fever – Jwara Nidana\n\n2 Chapter 2. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of Bleeding Disorders – Raktapitta Nidana\n\n3 Chapter 3. Diagnosis and etio-pathogenesis of Abdominal lumps – Gulma Nidana\n\n4 Chapter 4. Diagnosis and etiopatheogenesis of Obstinate Urinary Disorders including diabetes – Prameha Nidana\n\n5 Chapter 5. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of Skin diseases – Kushtha Nidana\n\n6 Chapter 6. Diagnosis and etiopatheogenesis of Progressive wasting disease- Shosha Nidana\n\n7 Chapter 7. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of psychosis disorders – Unmada Nidana\n\n8 Chapter 8. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of seizure disorders- Apasmara Nidana\n\nChapter 1. Chapter on Fundamental Principles of Diagnosis and Fever – Jwara Nidana\n\nChapter 2. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of Bleeding Disorders – Raktapitta Nidana\n\nChapter 3. Diagnosis and etio-pathogenesis of Abdominal lumps – Gulma Nidana\n\nChapter 4. Diagnosis and etiopatheogenesis of Obstinate Urinary Disorders including diabetes – Prameha Nidana\n\nChapter 5. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of Skin diseases – Kushtha Nidana\n\nChapter 6. Diagnosis and etiopatheogenesis of Progressive wasting disease- Shosha Nidana\n\nChapter 7. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of psychosis disorders – Unmada Nidana\n\nChapter 8. Diagnosis and etiopathogenesis of seizure disorders- Apasmara Nidana",
